    "q-130871": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130871",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2x}, & 1\\le x<e\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{x}{2}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{e}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-130871-a",
